# Player, Camera, and Input

Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: M1 Technical proofs
Dependencies: `01_PROJECT_FOUNDATION.todo`

## Purpose

Prove responsive third-person movement and visually honest aiming before territory complexity is added.

## Tasks

- [x] Implement camera-relative movement.
- [x] Implement acceleration, deceleration, gravity, and grounded state.
- [x] Implement independent camera look and aim.
- [x] Implement third-person camera collision.
- [x] Implement keyboard/mouse actions.
- [x] Implement gamepad actions.
- [x] Implement sensitivity and inversion settings.
- [x] Implement world-space aim solution.
- [x] Implement debug ray/contact visualization.
- [x] Define external impulse and status-modifier hooks.
- [x] Add movement and camera PlayMode tests.
- [x] Profile allocations and frame cost.
- [x] Add jump and wall-jump movement.
- [x] Add wall climbing.
- [x] Add a reduced-height character slide.
- [x] Add persistent pooled projectile impact splats.
- [x] Expand the sandbox with varied movement-test geometry.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Controller feels responsive in the sandbox at 60 FPS.
- [x] Reticle, physics contact, and spray target derive from the same aim solution.
- [x] Camera does not remain inside arena geometry.
- [x] Keyboard/mouse and gamepad are both usable.
- [x] No recurring managed allocation after warm-up.
- [x] Settings persist locally.

## Completion evidence

- Selected scene: `EntropyTag/Assets/EntropyTag/Scenes/Tests/Sandbox_PlayerMovement.unity`.
- Comparison scenes: eight variants under `EntropyTag/Assets/EntropyTag/Scenes/Tests/CameraVariants/`.
- EditMode: 4 passed, 0 failed.
- PlayMode: 10 passed, 0 failed.
- Warm player loop: zero managed allocation across 300 iterations; isolated average below 1 ms.
- Windows development build succeeded and excludes all eight comparison scenes.
- Documentation: `docs/11_PLAYER_CAMERA_INPUT.md`.
- Remaining gate: developer interactive feel check at 60 FPS.

## Completion log

- 2026-08-20 - Moved to IN_PROGRESS on `workDesk/agentic`. Added camera-relative CharacterController
  movement, acceleration/deceleration/gravity, camera orbit and sphere-cast collision, shared physics aim
  solution, keyboard/mouse and gamepad input consumption, persisted sensitivity/inversion settings, impulse
  and speed-modifier hooks, profiler diagnostics, a generated player sandbox, and initial tests.
- 2026-08-20 - Automated implementation validation passed at 00:56 IST: 3/3 EditMode, 5/5 PlayMode,
  zero-allocation warm-loop measurement, camera/aim/settings coverage, and successful Windows development
  build. Awaiting interactive movement/camera feel verification before DONE and commit.
- 2026-08-20 - The first feel check accepted WASD movement but rejected the centered reticle and shoulder
  camera shift. Replaced them with mouse/right-stick free aim, a central camera dead zone, edge-driven camera
  turn, and reticle-derived physics aiming. Revised validation passed at 01:27 IST: 4/4 EditMode, 5/5
  PlayMode, and Windows development build. Awaiting the second feel check.
- 2026-08-20 - The second feel check found the reticle faster than the camera and requested basic firing.
  Added smoothed reticle pursuit, damped faster camera edge turn, and a 24-object pooled sphere shooter using
  the shared aim solution. Validation passed at 02:09 IST: 4/4 EditMode, 6/6 PlayMode, and Windows build.
  Awaiting the third feel check.
- 2026-08-20 - The third feel check still found camera/reticle synchronization unsuitable. Added an Inspector
  `Camera Reticle Sync` multiplier with a live range of `0.25` to `4.0` so the developer can tune the relative
  camera catch-up speed and supply an accepted value.
- 2026-08-20 - Clarified the intended model: the crosshair remains fixed at screen center while mouse
  movement/right stick rotates the camera center directly; no shoulder shift and no free reticle. Replaced
  `FreeAimController` with `CenteredAimController`, exposing follow smoothing and speed. Validation passed at
  02:55 IST: 3/3 EditMode, 6/6 PlayMode, and Windows development build.
- 2026-08-20 - Paused at 03:06:29 IST without committing. Next step is an eight-scene comparative camera and
  crosshair study, including centered direct-follow and free-aim variants, followed by developer selection.
- 2026-08-21 - Resumed at 02:54:32 IST. Generated eight labeled comparison scenes using a shared experiment
  controller. All scenes keep movement, geometry, shooting, and the preferred cuboid-torso/sphere-head player
  placeholder constant while changing only camera/crosshair behavior.
- 2026-08-21 - Regenerated all eight scenes after adopting the cuboid-torso/sphere-head placeholder. Final
  automated validation passed 4/4 EditMode, 7/7 PlayMode, and the Windows development build. The only
  remaining acceptance gate is the developer's comparative 60 FPS playtest and camera-model selection.
- 2026-08-21 - Comparative feedback selected Variant 05, Free Aim Continuous Follow. Variants 01, 02, 03,
  and 08 showed firing-related camera collapse or flicker; 06 felt range-limited; 07's recentering overrode
  player intent; 04 was liked but 05 was preferred.
- 2026-08-21 - Promoted Variant 05 into `Sandbox_PlayerMovement`, excluded transient projectiles and splats
  from camera collision, and added jump, wall climb, wall jump, reduced-height slide, persistent pooled impact
  splats, a larger floor, climb wall, platform, ramp, beam, steps, and slide tunnel. Validation passed 4/4
  EditMode, 10/10 PlayMode, and the Windows development build. Final combined feel check remains open.
